diff --git a/docs/performance/setup-cleanup/memory-review/PLAN.md b/docs/performance/setup-cleanup/memory-review/PLAN.md
index 66a77abb5..e1ed1f748 100644
--- a/docs/performance/setup-cleanup/memory-review/PLAN.md
+++ b/docs/performance/setup-cleanup/memory-review/PLAN.md
@@ -13,3 +13,13 @@ Historical-provider reproduction and current-provider-PR-base validation are sep
 External process sampling interval: 5 ms during work. At phase checkpoints the guest process waits for an external smaps/status/fault/descriptor sample through two inherited pipes. Go counters are captured immediately before the handshake; report this observation delay. Record phase-specific sampled peaks and whole-process peak separately. Bound runs to 4,001 commands and a 512 MiB observed RSS stop limit; this stop is a diagnostic failure, not a sample to discard. Profiles use separate processes, including GODEBUG=memprofilerate=1 before package initialization for startup allocation attribution. No explicit GC or scavenging enters production.
 
 No production memory change is planned without new evidence. Preserve the fixed shared definitions and snapshot optimization unless a defect is demonstrated. Do not run the approximately 30 GiB all-engine screen for this focused review.
+
+Confirmation selected after the first current-base result, before new data: current-base tinyxml2 raw post-scavenge RSS increased by a paired mean 799.4 KiB (95% interval 232.2 to 1,340.0) while post-GC live heap changed by about 1 KiB. The historical session 1/2 RSS estimates do not consistently reproduce this. Run one separate current-base confirmation of exactly 20 pairs for tinyxml2/raw at normal, GC-only and scavenge endpoints, after the timing runs. Do not pool it with the first current-base sample or repeat it again to obtain significance. Examine anonymous mappings, released heap pages, stacks and file mappings.
+
+One timing confirmation is selected before further timing data: the current-base 1,024-host-call control increased 1.26% (p=0.001, n=20), while direct single-host-call time was unchanged and allocations were identical. Run exactly 20 additional pairs of the unchanged host-owned case in a fresh directory after the first timing comparisons and memory confirmation. Preserve both results separately; do not add samples or repeat again to obtain significance. No new production optimization is being proposed.
+
+Legacy replay correction: the first directory named historical-exact used a narrower corpus selection (only the target fixture, or cjson for minimal). The original runner always selected cjson,tinyxml2 before subtest selection; this changes untimed fixture loading and GC phase. Those existing samples remain valid for their recorded subset context but are invalid as an exact historical replay. Preserve them. Fix the legacy command and run a new, preselected 20-pair historical-full-context directory; do not combine the datasets. The new instrumented memory matrices intentionally select one target workload and are unaffected.
+
+Bounded host-call experiment: the PR table patch repeated a 1.26–1.75% slowdown in the 1,024-call control. AMD64 disassembly shows an additional stack copy when a concrete Caller is passed through the private stateFor HostModule parameter. Only the callback calls that method. An isolated one-line overlay narrows the private parameter to Caller without changing locks, error paths or handlers. The first 20-pair experiment improved 1,024 calls by 1.95% but increased the single-call control by 0.71%. Before accepting it, select exactly 20 new pairs of all focused/phases/host-owned controls against the existing optimized PR, plus the bounded memory matrix if timing supports acceptance. Do not pool or rerun this verification for significance. Reject the candidate if it does not preserve the direct-call control.
+
+Host candidate disposition: the fixed verification repeated the direct-call increase (+1.03%, p=0.003, 20 pairs), despite the heavy-call improvement (−1.96%). Reject the overlay. Do not run its conditional memory acceptance matrix or claim it passed correctness acceptance. Preserve both sessions.
